  {
   "approach": "Start at the Longs Peak Trailhead, on Highway 7, and follow the Longs Peak Trail to the Chasm Lake Trail; the lake is about 4.2 miles and 2,400 ft of gain from the trailhead. Skirt Chasm Lake on its north side (in winter the frozen lake can be crossed) to reach Mills Glacier beneath the east face, where Lamb's Slide begins. Reach Broadway by Lamb's Slide, which exits right onto the ledge, and traverse it to the feature you want. Joe's Solo begins from Broadway in a deep cleft, with the Notch Couloir on one side and The Eighth Route on the other.",
   "area_id": "co_long_s_peak_mt_meeker_cirque",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": "The quickest way down is the Loft. Another option is to rappel into the Notch and continue to the summit of Longs.",
