  {
   "approach": "Start at the Longs Peak Trailhead, on Highway 7, and follow the Longs Peak Trail to the Chasm Lake Trail; the lake is about 4.2 miles and 2,400 ft of gain from the trailhead. Skirt Chasm Lake on its north side (in winter the frozen lake can be crossed) to reach Mills Glacier beneath the east face, where Lamb's Slide begins. The Eighth Route is a broad gully sitting above Alexander's Chimney, immediately left of the Notch Couloir; reach it from Lamb's Slide or Broadway.",
   "area_id": "co_long_s_peak_mt_meeker_cirque",
   "descent": null,
   "descent_text": "At the top, either rappel into the Notch (the anchor is hard to locate) or walk off the back side and go down the Loft or Lamb's Slide.",
